      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ROLLING HOME (3) led and dug deep when challenged to score when fresh from a spell over this distance at Muswellbrook last start. Was gelded prior to that run and it has paid dividends. Expect him to keep progressing so another win is on the cards. NO NO YES (1) found Donatello, who was subsequently beaten narrowly in town, too strong when resuming over 1450m at Illawarra Grange last time out. Back in trip but did score impressively at the same time last prep over today's journey at Newcastle. Big chance despite the 61.5kgs impost. ADMIRE ME (7) is back from a six-month spell and has switched to the Scott Singleton yard. Didn't come up last prep but did win nicely on debut at Hawkesbury last November. Market watch advised. MAGURTZ (5) is back after a 136-day spell. Found 1000m too slick when resuming last prep then improved sharply when stepped up in distance. This looks a nice kick-off point. VALLE DI LUCE (6) resumes off a long break for a new stable. Keep an eye on the betting.",
